      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The skill contains examples that read and write local PDF files, but the metadata does not declare a least-privilege tool or filesystem scope. File I/O is expected for a PDF skill, which lowers suspicion, but the broad trigger plus unrestricted examples could lead an agent to read arbitrary user files, write outputs in unsafe locations, or overwrite files if not otherwise sandboxed.",
      "remediation": "Add explicit permissions/allowed-tools limiting access to user-provided PDFs and a dedicated working/output directory. Disallow network access and unrestricted shell use unless required, require user confirmation for overwrites, and validate/normalize paths to prevent traversal or accidental access outside the workspace.",
