        "end_line": 216
      },
      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The qpdf example shows removing PDF encryption/password protection without any authorization or privacy warning. Although qpdf requires the password and this is a legitimate operation in many workflows, stripping protections from PDFs can expose confidential documents or facilitate unauthorized redistribution.",
      "remediation": "Add an authorization warning before decryption/password-removal instructions: only decrypt PDFs the user owns or is explicitly authorized to modify, do not assist with password cracking or DRM bypass, and handle passwords securely. Prefer not to place passwords directly on command lines where they may appear in shell history or process listings; use safer prompting or protected variables where available.",
      "code_snippet": null,
